Issuer validation is controlled by:**\n- `verify_iss` option (default: `True`, see lines 33-42)\n- Passed via `issuer` parameter to `decode()`/`decode_complete()`\n\n### 3. JWT Libraries/Modules Found\n\nThe codebase is the **PyJWT library** itself (version 2.8.0) with these modules:\n\n| Module | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `api_jwt.py` | High-level JWT encoding/decoding |\n| `api_jws.py` | JSON Web Signature operations |\n| `api_jwk.py` | JSON Web Key operations |\n| `jwks_client.py` | JWKS (JWK Set) client for remote key fetching |\n| `algorithms.py` | Supported algorithms (HS256, RS256, etc.) |\n| `exceptions.py` | Custom exception classes |\n| `utils.py` | Utility functions (base64 encoding, etc.) |\n\n### Key Exception Classes (`/testbed/jwt/exceptions.py`)\n\n- `InvalidIssuerError` - When issuer doesn't match\n- `MissingRequiredClaimError` - When required claim (like 'iss') is missing\n- `DecodeError` - General decoding errors\n- `ExpiredSignatureError` - Token has expired\n- `InvalidSignatureError` - Signature verification failed\n\n### Default Verification Options (`/testbed/jwt/api_jwt.py` lines 33-42)\n\n```python\n{\n    \"verify_signature\": True,\n    \"verify_exp\": True,       # Expiration\n    \"verify_nbf\": True,       # Not Before\n    \"verify_iat\": True,       # Issued At\n    \"verify_aud\": True,       # Audience\n    \"verify_iss\": True,       # Issuer\n    \"require\": [],            # Required claims\n}\n```\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f99ffcac1ffeJinkVRwlideOn4","sessionId":"ses_f99ffc166ffeqL5pdaqkHevozE","model":{"modelID":"inception/mercury-2.5-preview","providerID":"openrouter"},"truncated":false},"title":"Find JWT validation code","time":{"start":1788417687197,"end":1788417697327}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_066003da1001Zxyyo5dFPuL8iJ","sessionID":"ses_f99ffcac1ffeJinkVRwlideOn4","messageID":"msg_066003757001Zcn8yduZH7kYWs"}}
