{"type":"text","timestamp":1788417741262,"sessionID":"ses_f99ffcac1ffeJinkVRwlideOn4","part":{"id":"prt_0660110da001StRHHpTob6jeal","messageID":"msg_066010cbc001ldfdsFLwex4I6U","sessionID":"ses_f99ffcac1ffeJinkVRwlideOn4","type":"text","text":"\n\nI've added support for validating JWT tokens with either a single issuer or multiple issuers. The changes are:\n\n1. **Modified `_validate_iss` method** in `/testbed/jwt/api_jwt.py` (line 358-372) to:\n   - Accept a single string as before\n   - Accept an iterable of strings for multiple issuers\n   - Validate that the token's `iss` claim matches any one of the provided issuers\n\n2. **Updated type hints** for the `issuer` parameter in both `decode` and `decode_complete` methods to indicate they now accept `str | Iterable[str] | None`\n\nAll existing tests pass, and the new functionality works as expected:\n- Single issuer strings work exactly as before\n- List of issuers validates the token if the `iss` claim matches any of them\n- Missing `iss` claim raises `MissingRequiredClaimError`\n- Invalid issuer (doesn't match) raises `InvalidIssuerError`","time":{"start":1788417741018,"end":1788417741260}}}
